     "\r\n<font face=\"georgia\" size=\"2\"><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>Dear all,</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>there are still 2 seats available for our upcoming online course: </span><strong><span>DNA Methylation in Ecology and Evolution.</span></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><strong><span>Course website: <a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/dnamethylation/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/dnamethylation/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230261205000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1oT-KSNGYrLM2DFk7XYbEH\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/dnamethylation/</a> </span></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><br><span>Dates: 20–24 April </span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>This\r\n course provides a practical introduction to the generation and analysis\r\n of DNA methylation data in ecology and evolution, with a focus on \r\nnon-model organisms.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>We will cover:</span></p>\r\n<ul><li><span>Short-read bisulfite sequencing (WGBS, EM-seq; Illumina)</span></li><li><span>Long-read approaches (Oxford Nanopore and PacBio)</span></li><li><span>Processing methylation data from raw reads to count matrices</span></li><li><span>Identification of differentially methylated sites and regions</span></li><li><span>Integration with SNP and gene expression data</span></li><li><span>Biological interpretation in ecological and evolutionary contexts</span></li></ul><p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>The\r\n course combines short lectures with extensive hands-on practical \r\nsessions, where participants will work directly with real datasets and \r\nanalysis pipelines.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>It\r\n is aimed at researchers and technical staff involved in generating or \r\nanalysing DNA methylation data, particularly in non-model organisms with\r\n available reference genomes.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"> </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span>Best regards,</span><br><span>Carlo</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:georgia;font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia;font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia;font-size:small\"></span></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;font-family:trebuchet ms;font-size:10pt\">--------------------<br><br>Carlo Pecoraro, Ph.D<br><br><br>Physalia-courses DIRECTOR<br><br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">in...@physalia-courses.org</a><br><br>mobile: <a href=\"tel:+49%20176%2045230846\" value=\"+4917645230846\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+49 17645230846</a><br><br><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/physaliacourses.bsky.social\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bsky.app/profile/physaliacourses.bsky.social&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230261205000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2kW8ss3VmylkBEIQYtPXR8\">Bluesky</a> <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/physalia-courses-a64418127/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" title=\"This external link will open in a new window\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.linkedin.com/in/physalia-courses-a64418127/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230261205000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3V7wo5lWUCcGAVZrn0sa_X\">Linkedin</a></p></font>\r\n\r\n<br>"
